<% content_for :full_screen do %>
<div class="chip-wrapper">

  <%= image_tag "chips.png", class: "chip-img" %>

  <!-- 🔥 BACK BUTTON HITBOX -->
  <%= link_to root_path, class: "chip-back-btn" do %>
  <% end %>

  <div class="chip-textbox">

    <p>
      I grew up in Milwaukee and somehow ended up in a tiny mountain town in Colorado, which feels pretty on brand for how my life has gone—unexpected turns, lots of learning, and a constant pull toward building things that matter.
    </p>

    <p>
      I’m a backend developer, project manager, linguist, and lifelong student. I’ve never really been just one thing, and I like it that way.
    </p>

    <p>
      Before I started writing code full-time, I was deep in the world of project management and IT consulting—working with teams at Xcel Energy, Sling TV, Crocs, and Sovos. I got really good at organizing chaos: Agile workflows, cloud migrations, SAP systems, and cross-functional teams with too many opinions and not enough alignment.
    </p>

    <p>
      Language has always been a huge part of my life too. I’m fluent in Spanish, and I spent time teaching English in Barcelona, which completely changed how I think about communication.
    </p>

    <p>
      Moving into backend development felt like a natural next step. At Turing, I leaned into building real applications—APIs, data models, and systems that actually <em>do</em> something.
    </p>

    <p>
      Outside of work, I’m usually making something—cooking, baking, experimenting, glass etching, or being outside in the mountains.
    </p>

    <p>
      That mix—technical, creative, a little unconventional—is kind of the through-line of everything I do.
    </p>

  </div>

</div>
<% end %>